{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/eval-INC-86-r1-instincts/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "The bug: `mustSegregate` strips the hazard division (e.g. `\"5.1\"` → `\"5\"`) via `primaryClass`, but the `SEGREGATION` table is keyed by full division-qualified classes (`\"5.1\"`, `\"5.2\"`, `\"2.1\"`, `\"4.1\"`). So any hazard class with a division never matches the table. `primaryClass` itself is correct and used elsewhere/tested as-is — the fix belongs in `mustSegregate`, which should look up by the full trimmed class, not the truncated primary.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9SGQp8cEQ8Z1as491F", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "16e7db7f-e95c-4073-bc6a-2dc66bec5e5f", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:42:53.698Z", "type": "assistant"}
