{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/eval-INC-86-r1-instincts/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "## Summary\n\nINC-86 was a bug in `src/cargo/hazmat.ts`: `mustSegregate` looked up hazard classes in the `SEGREGATION` table after stripping their division (e.g. `\"5.1\"` → `\"5\"` via `primaryClass`), but the table is keyed by full division-qualified classes (`\"5.1\"`, `\"5.2\"`, `\"2.1\"`, `\"4.1\"`). So any class with a division (oxidisers, organic peroxides, etc.) never matched, silently allowing incompatible cargo to be stowed adjacent.\n\nFixed `mustSegregate` to look up by the trimmed full class string instead of the truncated primary class (`primaryClass` itself is unchanged, since it's correctly used/tested elsewhere). Added test cases covering all the INC-86 acceptance pairs. Full suite (`npm run check`) passes: 27/27 tests.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9V96rfSMTxGwe8kDCd", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "16e7db7f-e95c-4073-bc6a-2dc66bec5e5f", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:43:23.343Z", "type": "assistant"}
